 34P     208PB(36S,XG):XUNDL-7         2015CH56                           201511
 34P  c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2015Ch56: Phys Rev C 92, 044308    
 34P 2c  (2015)                                                                 
 34P  c  Compiled by: J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), October 15, 2015                     
 34P  c  2015Ch56: E= 215 MeV {+36}S beam was produced using the combination    
 34P 2c  of XTU tandem Van de Graaff accelerator and ALPI superconducting       
 34P 3c  linear accelerator at the INFN Legnaro National Laboratory, Italy.     
 34P 4c  Target was 99.7% enriched {+208}Pb with a thickness of 300 |mg/cm{+2}  
 34P 5c  on a 20 |mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Fragments were separated and        
 34P 6c  identified by the PRISMA spectrometer and |g rays were detected with   
 34P 7c  the CLARA array of 25 EUROBALL escape-suppressed HPGe clover           
 34P 8c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g|g-coin. Deduced levels,  
 34P 9c  J,|p. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.                       
 34P  cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compiler)            
 34P  cL J$From Adopted Levels of {+34}P in ENSDF database, unless otherwise    
